  m_Name: 1946
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Return to British Rule and Growing Nationalism 1946 '
  info: 'After the Japanese surrender in 1945, Singapore returns to British control
    but is now directly governed as a separate Crown Colony. However, the war has
    left Singaporeans disillusioned with colonialism. A burgeoning nationalist movement
    emerges, with workers, unions, and political parties advocating for greater self-rule.
    Strikes and protests against poor wages and living conditions intensify, reflecting
    widespread dissatisfaction with British governance.  '
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: afe917992a9df41c1aba78e5e0f08221, type: 3}
